§ `Article 2(3): areas outside Union law, and military, defence and national security`

-- Under Article 2(3), as an importer, does the Regulation apply to the AI system used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes
-- 1 February 2025, Chapter I has not begun to apply, so nothing is covered (Art 113(a): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(3), as an importer, does the Regulation apply to the AI system used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes` (Date 1 2 2025) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, exclusively military, defence or national security: JUST FALSE ("This Regulation does not apply to AI systems where and in so far they are placed on the market, put into service, or used ... exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes")
-- MIRROR Art 2(3) second subparagraph: the same military AI system asked from each operator seat
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(3), as an importer, does the Regulation apply to the AI system used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 2 February 2025, a system with any other purpose too: NOTHING (limited by "exclusively")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(3), as an importer, does the Regulation apply to the AI system used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes` (Date 2 2 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 27 July 2026, the text as amended: JUST FALSE (the subparagraph was not changed)
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(3), as an importer, does the Regulation apply to the AI system used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes` (Date 27 7 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE


§ `Article 2(12): AI systems released under free and open-source licences`

-- Under Article 2(12), as an importer, does the Regulation apply to the AI system released under a free and open-source licence
-- 1 February 2025, Chapter I has not begun to apply, so nothing is covered (Art 113(a): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(12), as an importer, does the Regulation apply to the AI system released under a free and open-source licence` (Date 1 2 2025) TRUE `Route neither` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, open-source, not high-risk, outside Articles 5 and 50: JUST FALSE ("This Regulation does not apply to AI systems released under free and open-source licences")
-- MIRROR Art 2(12): the same open-source AI system asked from each operator seat
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(12), as an importer, does the Regulation apply to the AI system released under a free and open-source licence` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE `Route neither` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 2 February 2025, high-risk under Article 6(2) and Annex III: NOTHING ("unless they are placed on the market or put into service as high-risk AI systems")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(12), as an importer, does the Regulation apply to the AI system released under a free and open-source licence` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, high-risk under Article 6(1) and Annex I: NOTHING (the same "unless")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(12), as an importer, does the Regulation apply to the AI system released under a free and open-source licence` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE `Route Article 6(1) and Annex I` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, falls under Article 5: NOTHING ("or as an AI system that falls under Article 5")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(12), as an importer, does the Regulation apply to the AI system released under a free and open-source licence` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE `Route neither` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, falls under Article 50: NOTHING ("or 50")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(12), as an importer, does the Regulation apply to the AI system released under a free and open-source licence` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE `Route neither` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, not released under an open-source licence: NOTHING (the exclusion speaks of open-source systems only)
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(12), as an importer, does the Regulation apply to the AI system released under a free and open-source licence` (Date 2 2 2025) FALSE `Route neither` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 27 July 2026, the text as amended: JUST FALSE (paragraph 12 was not changed)
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(12), as an importer, does the Regulation apply to the AI system released under a free and open-source licence` (Date 27 7 2026) TRUE `Route neither` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE


