-- categorising biometric data in the area of law enforcement: 'does not cover'
#ASSERT `Under Article 5, as an importer, is my placing on the market of an AI system prohibited by Article 5(1)(g) (biometric categorisation to infer race, political opinions, trade union membership, religious or philosophical beliefs, sex life or sexual orientation)` (Date 3 2 2025) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the dataset does not relate to physical, physiological or behavioural characteristics, so it is not biometric data (Article 3(34)): the labelling carve-out does not apply
#ASSERT `Under Article 5, as an importer, is my placing on the market of an AI system prohibited by Article 5(1)(g) (biometric categorisation to infer race, political opinions, trade union membership, religious or philosophical beliefs, sex life or sexual orientation)` (Date 3 2 2025) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

